{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/44117-hedge-location-the-crucible","id":44117,"title":"Hedge Location: The Crucible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-07T06:17:42-08:00","id":44117,"title":"Hedge Location: The Crucible","content":"Deep, deep in the Hedge (though still in the Hedge\u2014it has to still be in the Hedge; Earth is far too static to ever effect such changes, and Arcadia is too dynamic for them to <i>last</i>) is a strange device: what appears to be a combination bellows and Bunsen burner, over which rests a large dome with a grate in one side, wherein sits a hole large enough for a person to lie down, all made of what looks like iron but can't be iron, not this far in the Hedge, not this close to Faerie. No, it must be some other metal that only looks and smells and feels like such.<br /> <br /> This is the Crucible. It can transform things, to an extent.<br /> <br /> Using the Crucible requires two people, one to operate the bellows, and one to be transformed. The potential transformee opens the hatch on the dome and crawls into the hole. The outside participant closes the hatch behind him, and takes up position and the handles of the metal bellows (which any student of metallurgy could tell you don't make any sense for this kind of device). Once in position, the bellows-operator gives a few good squeezes and un-squeezes, spending a point of Glamour in the process.<br /> <br /> This lights the fires of the Crucible. The bellows-operator's work is done, for now.<br /> <br /> Inside, once the fires are lit, the transformee can feel the flames ascending, heating his body, licking at his very essence. He now has some choices to make. In a single session inside the Crucible, a character can move around a number of dots in Attributes equal to his Wyrd within the same vertical or horizontal category. Maybe he wants to take the sharpness of his eyes and put it in his tongue instead. Or perhaps transmute muscle mass into harder bone.<br /> <br /> Anyone and anything with a Wyrd score, self-awareness, and attribute dots can be transformed by the Crucible. Changelings, True Fae Actors, hobgoblins, other, stranger entities. They are all fair game.<br /> <br /> (What happens if someone non-fae crawls into the Crucible? Best not to find out.)<br /> <br /> The entire process takes an hour, more or less. Usually more when greater amounts of attribute are being shuffled around, or the transformee is suddenly particularly undecisive. Less if the bellows-worker discovers that using such powerful magics this close to Arcadia draws the attention of curious Strangers. A few solid raps from inside the dome are a good indication that the transformee is done, and it's time to take him out.<br /> <br /> Such strange alchemy takes its toll on the character though. Even if he doesn't feel their pain completely, the soul-flames still scorch him, leaving invisible burns and a point of resistant Aggravated damage. It's not noticeable to the naked eye (though those who can see auras might take note of the singes around the edges of the transformed's) and doesn't come with most of the other implications of such harm (no loss of limbs, internal organ ruptures, etc), and it will heal naturally over time, but it definitely exists, and repeated trips to the Crucible could result in nothing more put a pile of ashes where once a best friend lay.<br /> <br /> If a changeling is the one inside the Crucible, such altering of the self is a Clarity 5 breaking point.<br /> <br /> One can keep going if one is unsatisfied. It just takes another point of Glamour for the bellows, another hour +/-, and another point of Aggravated damage from the fire if the transformee feels the need to make even more extensive changes.<br /> <br /> There are rumors that the Crucible is broken, incomplete. It doesn't look damaged, but from the right angle, with the right mindset, one could see where maybe certain pieces are missing, where additional supplementary devices could be installed. Maybe they're scattered around other parts of the Hedge or need to be forged or re-forged. Maybe the parts have to be stolen from Arcadia. With a more perfect Crucible, maybe it's possible to change one's appearance, Seeming, size. Maybe a changeling could use it to get his real soul back, or do <i>something</i> with a Fetch.<br /> <br /> Whence came the Crucible? Difficult to say. Autumn scholars in the know mostly posit it a relic spit out from Arcadia. Perhaps it's all that is left of a long-dead domain. Or perhaps, like all things Fae, the exact size of Arcadia is mutable, and the Crucible is flotsam from Faerie's receding tide (Lost of an overly optimistic bent might claim that this is proof that Arcadia is &quot;shrinking&quot; and, some era, will be gone forever). Maybe this is what the ancient Greek myth was talking about when recounting Prometheus stealing fire from the gods; maybe this strange machine was his actual gift to man, and somehow along the way it got lost in the Thorns. Or, maybe like all things in the Hedge, even though it sticks out like a sore thumb among all the greenery, the Crucible is just another naturally occurring madness. Maybe if you look into its heart you can find a metallic seed pod, ready to be transplanted and fertilized somewhere else.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T07:40:24-08:00","id":45583,"title":"","content":"Oh cool! Good job with the mystery! I like misc. stuff like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}